# Addresses the egress test (test_kind.py) probes for the ranges allowInternet's ipBlock excludes: one in each, none of them
# a cluster address (kind-calico.yaml puts pods in 10.244.0.0/16; Services are kind's 10.96.0.0/12;
# kind's docker network is a 172.x /16 that lan-targets.sh checks these avoid). lan-targets.sh makes
# each answer, from the kind host, so a block seen from a notebook pod is the policy and not an empty
# address. LAN_CONTROL is outside every excluded range: the notebook pod must reach it the same way.
# Copied from booth-streamlit (0e6b084).
LAN_PORT=18080
LAN_10=10.255.255.10
LAN_172=172.31.255.10
LAN_192=192.168.255.10
LAN_CGNAT=100.64.0.10
LAN_METADATA=169.254.169.254
LAN_CONTROL=198.51.100.10
